{
  "id": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
  "featureId": "ebb9ceb0-ea12-4374-af6e-12aa4256bcc3",
  "number": 85,
  "shortId": "WCF3E",
  "priority": 21,
  "slug": "components-declare-their-actions-chrome-focus-is-the-mode",
  "title": "Components declare their actions; chrome focus is the mode",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "A focused container receives the keyboard directly and runs actions IT declared — no generic verb set, no bespoke sidebar mode. Provider grows kind()/actions()/perform(); a row's nav_key is its one identity (cursor + right-click + drag); bindings live in [keys.<kind>], live only while focused. Retires InputMode::SidebarNav and the 11 sidebar_* built-ins.",
  "description": "# Why\n\nF003/P011/T020 landed chrome focus (a container id, a pick, a focus ring) and it is **inert**: nothing\ndelivers keys to a focused container, so `prefix+Shift+e` focuses a dock and then you still need\n`prefix+e` to do anything with it. Verdict from the user 2026-07-29: *\"it has no value if I have to do\nprefix+e to interact... it's only more keybindings.\"*\n\nAnd the thing it would generalise — `InputMode::SidebarNav` — is not generalisable as written: every\nverb in it is app code that knows the workspace tree. `handle_sidebar_up/down` drive\n`state.sidebar_tree` (a workspace/column/pane projection, `heca/src/handlers.rs:1562+`) and\n`handle_sidebar_right_nav` calls `handle_focus_pane` directly (`handlers.rs:1586`). A second container\ninherits none of it.\n\n# ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-29\n\n**The rule the design hangs on: widgets answer gestures; components declare semantics.**\n\n- Wheel, click, drag, hover, and keyboard **scrolling** are answered by the widgets a container\n  composes. `ScrollRegion` already answers the eight `WidgetIntent::Scroll*` and *declines* the axis it\n  cannot move (shipped `096f06e`). Nothing is declared for these — a container that nests a scroll area\n  scrolls; one showing a single number declines.\n- What only the component knows is **what its selection means**: rename *this*, delete *this*, restart\n  *this*. That is what it declares.\n\n**No generic verb set.** An inherited up/down/select/toggle vocabulary is dead weight for a container\nshowing one number — \"a component knows exactly what it needs\" (user). Conventional *ids* (`up`,\n`down`, `activate`, `remove`, `add`) are encouraged so docks agree in practice, never enforced in code.\n\n**Focus is the mode.** No `InputMode` variant for it: chrome focus already answers \"where do the keys\ngo\", and a mode beside it would be a second fact that can disagree (the defect `nav_selection` vs\n`sidebar_tree.cursor` already paid for). Key routing, top to bottom, in every focus state:\n\n1. prefix key → prefix mode → mode triggers → the global `normal` map → **falls through to the focused\n   component's layer** → drop\n2. global direct bindings (`Alt+Enter`, `Shift+PageUp`, …)\n3. if a component holds chrome focus → its `[keys.<kind>]` layer → **swallow** if unbound\n4. otherwise → forward to the focused pane's backend\n\n`state.focused_pane` is NOT cleared by chrome focus — only the keyboard is redirected, so `prefix+Enter`\nstill splits the pane you last worked in, exactly as sidebar mode behaves today.\n\n**Components declare, mostly bind.** A component's keymap maps keys to **any** action id — an existing\nbuilt-in (`next_pane`, `zoom_column`, `spawn_command` with args) or one of its own registered ids. It\ndeclares only what does not exist yet, which is the selection-dependent handful.\n\n**`perform`, not one closure per action.** `Provider` gains `perform(id, args, cx) -> Handled`: it is\nthe shape a WASM component is forced into (an id + args crosses a boundary, a closure does not), it\nkeeps `&self` available, and `ProviderCx` (read + emit) enforces §2.3 — a raw `DynHandler` hands a\ncomponent `&mut AppState`, which is more power than a provider may have.\n\n**A row's `nav_key` is its one identity.** Not a keyboard concern: the keyboard cursor, the right-click\ntarget, and (later) drag are three readers of the same declaration. The host derives the context path\nfrom the owning component's `kind()`.\n\n**kind vs mount.** Bindings and declared actions belong to the component **type** (`kind()`, the config\nnamespace `[keys.docker]`); cursor, scroll offset and focus belong to each **placement** (`id()`, the\nmount). `Hero::new()` twice = two instances of one type. `WorkspacesContainerProvider::placed(id,\nregion)` currently makes `id()` the mount id with no `kind()`, so this must land before a second\nplacement exists.\n\n# The worked example — a Docker containers dock, end to end\n\nTwo actions only it can do, three keys (one reusing a built-in with args), right-click firing one of\nthem. ✦ marks API this phase adds.\n\n## The component\n\n```rust\n// heca/src/providers/docker.rs — app-side. A WASM plugin is the same shape across the boundary.\n\npub struct DockerProvider {\n    /// This PLACEMENT (`docker`, `docker.right`). Cursor/scroll/focus key off this.\n    id: String,\n    region: RegionId,\n    /// The component's own domain state — not app state.\n    service: DockerService,\n}\n\nimpl Provider for DockerProvider {\n    fn id(&self) -> &str { &self.id }          // instance\n    fn kind(&self) -> &str { \"docker\" }        // ✦ TYPE → the config namespace `[keys.docker]`\n    fn title(&self) -> &str { \"Containers\" }\n    fn supported_regions(&self) -> RegionSet { RegionSet::sidebars() }\n    fn default_region(&self) -> RegionId { self.region }\n    fn keyboard_navigable(&self) -> bool { true }\n\n    fn build_contribution(&self, ctx: &ChromeCtx<'_>) -> Contribution {\n        Contribution::Container(ContainerContribution { /* … */ build: Box::new(build_body) })\n    }\n}\n\nfn build_body(ctx: &ChromeCtx<'_>, bx: &mut BuildCx<'_>) -> WidgetModel {\n    let mut list = Flex::column().gap(4.0);\n    for c in ctx.state().containers::<DockerRow>() {\n        list = list.child(\n            Row::new()\n                .nav_key(&c.id)        // ✦ the row's ONE identity: cursor + right-click target (+ drag later)\n                .on_activate(/* click = attach */)\n                .child(Label::new(&c.name)),\n        );\n    }\n    // Scrolling is the widget's: nested here, it answers PageUp/Down/Home/End with nothing declared.\n    Box::new(ScrollRegion::new().grow(1.0).child(list))\n}\n```\n\n## Its two actions ✦\n\n```rust\nimpl ProviderActions for DockerProvider {\n    /// ONLY what nothing else can do. Everything else it wants is an existing action it binds.\n    fn actions(&self) -> Vec<ActionMeta> {\n        vec![\n            ActionMeta {\n                name: \"docker.restart_selected\".into(),\n                label: \"Restart Container\".into(),\n                description: \"Restart the selected container.\".into(),\n                category: ActionCategory::Chrome,\n                default_binding: \"r\".into(),      // the field already exists — unused today\n                icon: Some(Glyph::ArrowClockwise),\n                policy: ActionPolicy::Global,\n                args: vec![],                      // acts on the selection; nothing to pass\n                confirm: None,\n            },\n            ActionMeta {\n                name: \"docker.stop_selected\".into(),\n                label: \"Stop Container\".into(),\n                description: \"Stop the selected container.\".into(),\n                category: ActionCategory::Chrome,\n                default_binding: \"s\".into(),\n                icon: Some(Glyph::Stop),\n                policy: ActionPolicy::Global,\n                args: vec![],\n                // Destructive → the CENTRAL confirm gate prompts on every surface. Free.\n                confirm: Some(ConfirmSpec::destructive(\"docker_stop\", \"Stop\")),\n            },\n        ]\n    }\n\n    /// One entry point. The selection is the component's own, keyed by THIS mount.\n    fn perform(&self, action: &str, _args: &Intent, cx: &mut ProviderCx<'_>) -> Handled {\n        let Some(id) = cx.selected() else { return Handled::No };   // nothing selected ⇒ decline\n        match action {\n            \"docker.restart_selected\" => { self.service.restart(id); Handled::Yes }\n            \"docker.stop_selected\"    => { self.service.stop(id);    Handled::Yes }\n            _ => Handled::No,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`perform` never touches `AppState`: its own service, or `cx.dispatch(\"focus_pane\", args)` to reach an\napp action.\n\n## Its three keybindings — shipped defaults, live only while it has focus\n\n```toml\n# keybindings.default.toml\n[keys.docker]                 # ✦ merges PER KEY: override one, keep the rest\nrestart_selected = \"r\"        # its own action (namespace implied by the table)\nstop_selected    = \"s\"\n\n[[keys.docker.bind]]          # ✦ the arg-carrying form; merges by `keys`\naction = \"spawn_command\"      # ← an EXISTING built-in, not redeclared\nkeys   = \"t\"\nargs   = { command = \"lazydocker\", float = \"true\" }\n\n[keys.docker.unbind]          # ✦ explicit removal (no null/empty-string semantics)\n\"s\" = true\n```\n\n## Right-click → the same action\n\n```rust\nfn context_menus(&self, _ctx: &ChromeCtx<'_>) -> Vec<ContextMenuContribution> {\n    vec![ContextMenuContribution {\n        context_path: \"container.docker\".into(),   // derived from kind() on the resolution side\n        weight: vec![1],\n        build: Box::new(|_ctx, target| vec![\n            MenuEntry::action(\"Restart\", Intent::new(\"docker.restart_selected\"))\n                .enabled(target.row_key().is_some()),\n            MenuEntry::action(\"Stop\", Intent::new(\"docker.stop_selected\")),\n        ]),\n    }]\n}\n```\n\nSame id, same `perform`, same confirm gate — one path for key, menu and RPC. The hook exists today\n(`Provider::context_menus`); `row_key()` on the target is new.\n\n## The one host-side piece\n\n```rust\n// on mount, once — the HOST, not the component (a provider never mutates app state)\nfor meta in provider.actions() {\n    let kind = provider.kind().to_string();\n    let default_keys = meta.default_binding.clone();\n    let id = meta.name.clone();\n    handles.keep(register_dynamic(registry, catalog, meta, Some(Rc::new(route_to_owner))));\n    keymaps.bind_component_default(&kind, &default_keys, &id);   // ✦ user config wins\n}\n\n// and the bridge, written once for every component that will ever exist\nfn route_to_owner(state: &mut AppState, intent: &Intent) {\n    let Some(mount) = owning_mount(state, &intent.action) else { return };  // focused, else last-focused of that kind\n    let store = state.chrome_state.clone();        // Rc alias — no borrow of AppState held\n    let mut cx = ProviderCx::new(&mount, store, state.intent_sink());\n    if let Some(p) = state.chrome_host.provider(&mount) {\n        p.perform(&intent.action, intent, &mut cx);  // &self available; no &mut AppState alive\n    }\n    cx.drain_into(state);                          // emitted intents applied by the host\n}\n```\n\n## What the author wrote vs what they got\n\n**Written:** `kind()`, two `ActionMeta`s, a five-line `perform`, `.nav_key()` per row, three TOML\nlines, one menu hook.\n\n**Free:** the palette entry with its icon and label; `describe-action` + RPC; the destructive confirm\non every surface; `prefix+/` hint targets on the rows; wheel, click, drag and PageUp/Down/Home/End from\nthe widgets; the focus ring; a cursor that survives a tree rebuild.\n\n**Written nowhere:** up/down/select verbs — for this component they are the cursor over its own\n`nav_key`ed rows; for a one-number component they do not exist.\n\n# What already exists and is unused\n\n- `register_dynamic(registry, catalog, meta, handler)` (`heca/src/actions.rs:409`) — name-keyed actions\n  joining the same catalog as built-ins: label, icon, `policy`, declared `args`, `confirm`. Carries\n  `ActionMeta.default_binding` (`actions.rs:2072`) which is **`#[allow(dead_code)]` — declared, never\n  consumed by anything**.\n- `DynHandler = Rc<dyn Fn(&mut AppState, &Intent)>` (`actions.rs:377`); `handler: None` =\n  `Dispatch::Declarative`, already how a WASM action is modelled.\n- `ProviderHandles` (`heca/src/providers/mod.rs:100`) — documented as where dynamic-action unregister\n  handles join, so actions dying with the mount is the intended lifetime.\n- `Provider::context_menus` (`providers/mod.rs:83`) is live: right-click / `prefix+>` →\n  `open_context_menu_for` (`chrome/context_menu.rs:232`) → `plugin_providers_for` (`:271`) →\n  `host.mounted_providers().flat_map(|p| p.context_menus(ctx))` filtered by `context_path`.\n- Config bindings already resolve to `ActionRef::Builtin` **or** `ActionRef::Dynamic` at press\n  (`app/registry.rs`), so binding a component's id needs no new resolution.\n- `FocusRing` + `focused_container` + per-mount `keyboard_target` signals + the `focus_dock` pick\n  (F003/P011/T020, landed).\n\n# The gap, precisely\n\n- Nothing turns `ActionMeta.default_binding` into a binding (the keymap is built from config at load,\n  before any provider activates).\n- Nothing scopes a binding to \"while this component has focus\".\n- Right-click resolves its `(ContextPath, ContextTarget)` by **matching a closed domain enum**:\n  `mouse.rs:143` matches `ChromeDragItem::{Pane,Column,Workspace}`, and `ContextTarget` is closed too.\n  A plugin row cannot be expressed, so a `container.docker` path could never be produced.\n- `resolve_active_context` (`context_menu.rs:308`) reads `InputMode::SidebarNav` + the sidebar cursor —\n  a second, keyboard-specific resolution of the same fact.\n\n# Decisions, dated (do not re-open without the user)\n\n| Decision | Date |\n|---|---|\n| Widgets answer gestures; components declare semantics | 2026-07-29 |\n| No generic verb set — a component declares exactly what it needs; conventional ids encouraged, never enforced | 2026-07-29 |\n| Focus is the mode — no `InputMode` variant beside it | 2026-07-29 |\n| An unbound key while a component is focused is **swallowed**, never forwarded to the backend | 2026-07-29 |\n| Prefix **falls through** to the focused component's layer when the global map misses | 2026-07-29 |\n| `perform(id, args, cx)`, not one closure per action | 2026-07-29 |\n| `kind()` (type → bindings, declared actions) is distinct from `id()` (mount → cursor, scroll, focus) | 2026-07-29 |\n| `nav_key` is the row's one identity: cursor, right-click target, later drag | 2026-07-29 |\n| `[keys.<kind>]` is a TABLE (merges per key); `[[keys.<kind>.bind]]` merges by `keys`; removal via an explicit `unbind` table, never null/empty-string | 2026-07-29 |\n| The palette/RPC show every registered action; choosing one focuses its component then performs (`FocusContainerThenAction`), with the last-focused instance of that kind as the target | 2026-07-29 |\n| An `ActionDispatched` event is a **notification**, not a veto | 2026-07-29 |\n| Keyboard scrolling is the widget's — no declaration; plain PageUp/Down/Home/End while focused, superseding T012's prefix-gated route | 2026-07-29 |\n\n# Acceptance for the phase\n\n- A container declaring nothing still scrolls, clicks and drags; a container declaring two actions gets\n  keys, RPC, palette, context menu and the confirm gate from that declaration alone.\n- No generic verb set anywhere; no `InputMode::SidebarNav`; no `sidebar_*` built-ins.\n- Nothing in the focus, menu or nav path matches on a workspace/column/pane enum.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings, and the USER drives it in the app (this is interaction —\n  tests are not verification).",
