    {
      "id": "3752b13d-8b2f-48a1-98c9-95408f78c0f7",
      "phaseId": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
      "number": 352,
      "shortId": "VKF85",
      "priority": 2,
      "shortName": "focus-is-the-mode-route-the-ke",
      "title": "Focus is the mode: route the keyboard to the focused component (absorbs the keyboard-scroll task)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "# What\n\nMake chrome focus decide where unprefixed keys go. No `InputMode` variant: focus is already the fact,\nand a mode beside it would be a second one that can disagree.\n\n**This task absorbs CY8C2** (\"ScrollRegion keyboard-scroll actions\", canceled 2026-07-30 at the user's\nrequest — they said the same thing). Everything CY8C2 still carried is transferred below, verbatim\nwhere it is still true.\n\n# Current state\n\n`handle_keyboard_input` (`heca/src/app/input.rs:34`): `InputMode::Normal` forwards every unbound key to\nthe focused pane's backend (`:58-88`) after trying the `global` keymap. Prefix mode\n(`handle_prefix_mode`, `:208`) resolves mode triggers, then the `normal` map, then **drops** the key\n(`:275` — the `else if !ctx.key_text.is_empty()` arm just exits prefix). `InputMode::SidebarNav` is a\nbespoke arm delegating to the `\"sidebar\"` mode keymap (`handle_sidebar_nav_mode`, `:584`).\n\n# ✅ DECIDED — the order, in every focus state\n\n1. prefix key → prefix mode → mode triggers → global `normal` map → **falls through to the focused\n   component's `[keys.<kind>]` layer** (user decision 2026-07-29) → drop\n2. global direct bindings (`Alt+Enter`, `Shift+PageUp`, …) — unchanged\n3. **if a component holds chrome focus** → its layer → **swallow** if unbound (user decision: a `j`\n   leaking into a shell is the worse failure)\n4. otherwise → forward to the focused pane's backend, as today\n\n`state.focused_pane` is **not** cleared: chrome focus redirects the keyboard, nothing else, so\n`prefix+Enter` still splits the pane you last worked in.\n\n# Steps\n\n1. One branch at the top of the `InputMode::Normal` arm: chrome focus set ⇒ resolve in the component\n   layer, else the existing terminal-forward path. Unbound ⇒ consume (do not forward).\n2. Prefix fall-through: after the `normal` map misses, try the focused component's layer before\n   dropping.\n3. Suppress the **double-prefix literal forward** (`prefix_combo_to_literal_input`, `input.rs:224`)\n   while a component has focus — nothing there is receiving text, so sending a literal `Ctrl+B` to a\n   pane the user is not typing in is a surprise.\n4. `Esc` returns focus to the pane (clear `focused_container`); `focus_dock` aimed at the\n   already-focused dock toggles focus back off.\n5. Status bar: derive the mode word from the focused component's `title()` (`status_mode_parts`,\n   `app/render.rs:54`) so unprefixed keys never go somewhere invisible. The focus ring is the other\n   half of that guardrail.\n\n# Keyboard scrolling (was CY8C2)\n\n## ✅ SHIPPED — the widget half (`096f06e`), unchanged by anything here\n\nEight `WidgetIntent` variants: `ScrollPageUp` / `ScrollPageDown` / `ScrollToTop` / `ScrollToBottom`\nand the four horizontal ones. `ScrollRegion` acts on them:\n\n- it owns the arithmetic — a page is 0.9 of its viewport, the edges clamp — because it is the only\n  thing that knows its viewport and its content;\n- it **declines** an axis it cannot scroll (axis off, or content fits), so a nested region or the host\n  gets a turn; consuming would make the key silently do nothing;\n- handled after the children, so the innermost scrollable region wins, as with the wheel;\n- `keyboard_target(Signal<bool>)` gates which instance responds — per instance, position-agnostic,\n  unset means yes. Bound to the mount's chrome focus by F003/P011/T020\n  (`StateView::container_keyboard_target`).\n\n**The logic lives in the widget, once.** Every `ScrollRegion` anywhere — any container, any nesting\ndepth, any region, any one added later — behaves identically with no per-usage code. That is the\nstanding requirement (user, 2026-07-28): *a widget holds its logic like a React component; move it\naround the app and it works the same, without reinventing anything.* The host will only ever say\n\"one page down, this axis\"; the widget decides everything else.\n\n## ⚠️ THE ROUTE CHANGED — 2026-07-29, by the user. This supersedes the 2026-07-16/27 keys.\n\n**Superseded:** vertical `prefix+Home/End/PageUp/PageDown`, horizontal `prefix+Shift+` the same four.\nThat shape existed only because there was no other way to stop the keys reaching the terminal.\n\n**Now:** while a component holds chrome focus nothing is forwarded to a backend, so **plain\n`PageUp` / `PageDown` / `Home` / `End` are free** and are the container's scroll keys; the existing\n`Shift+` variants stay exactly as they are for the focused *pane*'s scrollback.\n\n## The work\n\n6. The bindings already exist and are already global/direct: `scroll_page_up = \"Shift+PageUp\"`,\n   `scroll_page_down`, `scroll_to_top = \"Shift+Home\"`, `scroll_to_bottom = \"Shift+End\"`,\n   `scroll_line_up/down` (`keybindings.default.toml`), handled today against the focused terminal\n   viewport. **One branch at the top of those existing handlers**: chrome focus set ⇒ dispatch the\n   matching `Event::Widget(WidgetIntent::Scroll*)` into the chrome tree — the FocusScope (P085/T351)\n   delivers it to the focused container and every other container is inert — else the terminal\n   viewport path, unchanged. One binding, one meaning: *scroll whatever has focus*.\n7. **The four horizontal actions** still need adding (`ScrollPageLeft/Right`,\n   `ScrollToLeftEdge/RightEdge` — the widget intents exist, no `WmAction` does), through the full\n   Adding-New-Actions checklist (AGENTS.md): variant → `action_from_name` → `action_priority` →\n   `action_policy()` → handler → `build_registry` → `keybindings.default.toml` → `ActionRegistry::ALL`\n   descriptor **with its `args` declaration** → `rpc.rs` → README. Reuse `ResizeAxis`\n   (`heca/src/input.rs:40`, `EnumArg::VALUES = [\"x\",\"horizontal\",\"width\",\"y\",\"vertical\",\"height\"]`) if\n   an axis argument is preferred over four names — optional, defaulting to vertical, so a plain binding\n   stays legal (a *required* argument would forbid a bare key, F003/P010/T006).\n8. A **declined** intent (`Handled::No` — e.g. a container with nothing scrollable) stops at the\n   chrome; it does **not** fall through to the pane. The innermost-wins rule is about nested *scroll\n   areas*, and the pane is not an outer scroll area of the sidebar.\n\n## Still ruled out (2026-07-28, checked in code — do not re-open)\n\nFeeding these through the **widget keymap** (`build_widget_keymap`, `heca/src/app/registry.rs:202`,\nthe `[keys.widgets]` config table that `Input`/`Select`/`Tabs`/`Dialog` use). It is consulted at\n`heca/src/app/events.rs:156` inside a branch that requires **a modal to be open** and the mode *not* to\nbe `Prefix`/`HintPick` — so `[keys.widgets]` reaches focused widgets **inside modals only**. Do not add\na widget-keymap path beside the actions: it would be a second way to do one thing.\n\n## The 2026-07-17 blocker is discharged\n\n\"No chrome surface mounts a `ScrollRegion`\" is false since 2026-07-26: containers nest their own\n(`heca/src/providers/workspaces.rs`). `GridKey` still has no `PageUp`/`PageDown` — and does not need\nit, because the intent is semantic. That is the point of not delivering a key.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- Prefix, hint pick, and every mode trigger must keep working while a component is focused (they are\n  resolved first, by construction).\n- A pick mode (`DockPick`, `PaneSelect`, …) is entered *from* a focused component and must still\n  resolve normally.\n- Nothing may reach a backend while chrome focus is set — audit every `process_input` call on the\n  Normal path.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- With a dock focused: its keys work unprefixed, `prefix+…` still works, unbound keys do nothing, and\n  nothing reaches the terminal.\n- Plain `PageUp`/`PageDown`/`Home`/`End` scroll the focused dock; the same keys with `Shift` still\n  scroll the focused pane when no dock is focused. Every other scroll area declines.\n- Horizontal scrolling reachable from RPC through the same actions, one code path.\n- No second mechanism for the same job.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings. **The USER drives it in the app** — this is interaction,\n  with more than one scroll area on screen (P085(F007)/T359 seats the second one).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "3752b13d-8b2f-48a1-98c9-95408f78c0f7-check-001-in-progress-done",
          "date": "2026-07-29T09:57:49.013Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "done",
          "title": "Verified in the app by the user 2026-07-29: focus and cursor movement work. Chrome focus routes the keyboard, the focus layer resolves, and the dock scrolls. The known remaining defect on this path — Space handing the keyboard to the pane instead of keeping it on the dock — is F003/P086/T364, not this task.",
          "description": "Verified in the app by the user 2026-07-29: focus and cursor movement work. Chrome focus routes the keyboard, the focus layer resolves, and the dock scrolls. The known remaining defect on this path — Space handing the keyboard to the pane instead of keeping it on the dock — is F003/P086/T364, not this task."
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
