    {
      "id": "b1e0e7b5-b372-40bd-89be-fd3343729474",
      "phaseId": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
      "number": 355,
      "shortId": "NH962",
      "priority": 5,
      "shortName": "keys-lt-kind-gt-a-component-s",
      "title": "Per-kind keybindings: a component's bindings, merged by key, live only while it is focused",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "# What\n\nPer-component keymaps: shipped defaults, user-overridable one key at a time, resolved only while that\ncomponent holds chrome focus.\n\n# Current state\n\n- The keymap is built from config **at load** (`build_keymap`, `heca/src/app/registry.rs`), before any\n  provider activates — so a declared `ActionMeta.default_binding` (`actions.rs:2072`,\n  `#[allow(dead_code)]`) reaches nothing today.\n- Config merge rules (AGENTS § Config Loading): tables merge **per key**; scalars and **arrays are\n  replaced wholesale**. That is why `[[keys.mode]]` blocks have to be merged back by name at runtime\n  (`build_modes`) — a user redefining one mode would otherwise lose the built-ins.\n- `action_ref_from_config(name, args)` already resolves a name to `ActionRef::Builtin` **or**\n  `ActionRef::Dynamic` at press, so binding a component's own id needs no new resolution.\n- `[keys.unbind]` already removes a binding **by key combo**, \"whatever it points at\".\n\n# ✅ DECIDED — the shape\n\n```toml\n[keys.docker]                 # a TABLE: merges per key, so overriding one keeps the rest\nrestart_selected = \"r\"        # the component's own action (its kind namespaces it)\nstop_selected    = \"s\"\nfocus_next_pane  = \"n\"        # ← an EXISTING built-in, just bound here\n\n[[keys.docker.bind]]          # the arg-carrying form — arrays are otherwise replaced wholesale,\naction = \"spawn_command\"      #   so these merge by their `keys` field (a keymap IS a map from\nkeys   = \"t\"                  #   combo to action; merging on the combo is not a special case)\nargs   = { command = \"lazydocker\", float = \"true\" }\n\n[keys.docker.unbind]          # explicit removal — NOT null/empty-string semantics (the program\n\"s\" = true                    #   catalog uses `disabled = true` for the same reason)\n```\n\n# Steps\n\n1. Parse `[keys.<kind>]` (table), `[[keys.<kind>.bind]]` (array, merged by `keys`) and\n   `[keys.<kind>.unbind]` in `heca-config` beside the existing `[keys]`/`[[keys.mode]]` handling.\n2. Merge-by-key for the array form: a user entry with the same `keys` replaces the default's; everything\n   else survives. This is the fix that makes the arg-carrying form usable at all.\n3. **Bind declared defaults at mount** (`bind_component_default`): after a provider's actions are\n   registered, bind each `ActionMeta.default_binding` into that kind's layer **unless the user already\n   bound that key or rebound that action id** — user config always wins, and a default never silently\n   shadows one.\n4. Resolution: while a component holds chrome focus, its layer is consulted (see the routing task).\n   Built-in components ship their defaults in `keybindings.default.toml` so the defaults stay\n   discoverable (AGENTS: a default that lives only in code is a bug); a **plugin** has no line in that\n   file, so its manifest is the source there, with user config still winning.\n5. Document both in `README.md` and `keybindings.default.toml`, including the merge-by-key rule and\n   `unbind`.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- A binding to an id whose component is not mounted is **not** an error (config is read before\n  providers register — the existing `ActionRef::Dynamic` rule): it simply does nothing until the\n  component appears.\n- Two placements of one kind share the layer (bindings belong to the type; only state is per mount).\n- A component that declares no actions and binds nothing needs no table at all.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- `[keys.docker] stop_selected = \"x\"` changes one key and keeps `r` and `t`.\n- `[[keys.docker.bind]]` with `keys = \"t\"` replaces exactly that default and keeps the others.\n- `ActionMeta.default_binding` is no longer dead code.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "b1e0e7b5-b372-40bd-89be-fd3343729474-check-001-in-progress-done",
          "date": "2026-07-29T09:51:36.891Z",
          "fromStatus": "in-progress",
          "toStatus": "done",
          "title": "Built and green (69b4158): per-kind layers, merge-by-key for the table, merge-by-keys for the arg-carrying array, unbind by combo, and default_binding consumed at mount. The config SHAPE is replaced by F003/P086/T362 ([[keys.component]] with name + id) and default_binding is deleted by F003/P086/T366 — but the work under this task was completed as specified, and its merge rules carry over unchanged.",
          "description": "Built and green (69b4158): per-kind layers, merge-by-key for the table, merge-by-keys for the arg-carrying array, unbind by combo, and default_binding consumed at mount. The config SHAPE is replaced by F003/P086/T362 ([[keys.component]] with name + id) and default_binding is deleted by F003/P086/T366 — but the work under this task was completed as specified, and its merge rules carry over unchanged."
        }
      ],
