    },
    {
      "id": "95ef84f9-7def-4c4e-8032-f87d583faac8",
      "phaseId": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
      "number": 358,
      "shortId": "ABFAU",
      "priority": 8,
      "shortName": "palette-and-rpc-reach-a-compon",
      "title": "Palette and RPC reach a component's actions from anywhere: FocusContainerThenAction",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "# What\n\nA declared action must be usable without first focusing its component by hand — from the command\npalette, from RPC, from a menu — while still meaning something (a selection-dependent action needs its\ncomponent to be the focused one).\n\n# ✅ DECIDED (user question 2026-07-29: \"what will the command palette discover?\")\n\n**Everything registered, and registration follows mounting.** A component's actions enter the catalog\non mount and are retired with it (`ProviderHandles` + `unregister_dynamic`), so an action for a\ncomponent that is not mounted simply does not exist — no filtering needed, it falls out.\n\n**Mounted but unfocused: still shown.** Choosing one focuses its component and then performs, using the\nprecedent already in the codebase for exactly this problem: pane-header buttons whose action needs the\npane focused register `InteractionIntent::FocusPaneThenAction { pane_id, action }`, which\n`dispatch_intent` expands into focus-then-act (`heca/src/app/interaction.rs`, and see AGENTS §\n\"Active-targeted buttons must focus first\").\n\n# Steps\n\n1. `InteractionIntent::FocusContainerThenAction { container, action }`, expanded in `dispatch_intent`\n   into `FocusDock { dock } ` + the action — mirroring `FocusPaneThenAction` exactly.\n2. Palette entries for component actions carry it, and are labelled with their scope:\n   `\"Containers › Restart Container\"` — the component's `title()` + the action's `label`, both already\n   in metadata. The focused component's actions sort first; nothing is hidden.\n3. **Which instance**, when a kind is mounted twice: the last-focused instance of that kind, else the\n   first mounted. One rule, written down once (`owning_mount`, shared with the `perform` bridge) rather\n   than decided per call site.\n4. RPC: the same resolution, plus an explicit override for scripts — `--dock docker.right` — so a script\n   can target a specific placement without focusing it first.\n5. `list-actions` / `describe-action` include component actions with their owner, so introspection shows\n   who owns what.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- A selection-dependent action chosen from the palette with nothing selected: `perform` declines\n  silently after focusing. Acceptable for now; a later optional `can_perform(&self, id) -> bool` would\n  drive a disabled entry (menu entries already have an enabled state). **Do not build it now.**\n- An action id whose component was unmounted between the palette opening and the choice: resolve to\n  nothing and say so, rather than dispatching into the void.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- Searching the palette finds `Restart Container` while the Docker dock is mounted and unfocused;\n  choosing it focuses that dock and restarts.\n- `heca action docker.stop_selected` works from a script, with `--dock` to disambiguate two placements.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-28T12:25:38.894Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T12:25:38.894Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "93e90146-83e1-453d-a443-05dc03b325bd",
      "phaseId": "5de43f15-8304-4f64-870f-8514d534d5a5",
      "number": 359,
      "shortId": "J88GP",
      "priority": 9,
      "shortName": "two-containers-on-screen-the-r",
      "title": "Two containers on screen: the right sidebar comes back as the verification bed",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "# What\n\nSeat a second container so the whole phase can actually be demonstrated, and so the kind/mount split is\nexercised by something real rather than by a test.\n\n# ✅ DECIDED BY THE USER 2026-07-29 — this reverses the 2026-07-28 \"the test bed stays gone\"\n\n*\"for this test would be good to have the right sidebar with the workspaces you removed.\"* The earlier\ndecision (F003/P011/T021, commit `95a894d`) removed two extra placements because they were scaffolding\nwith nothing to prove. There is now something to prove: with **one** container on screen none of this\nphase is observable — not a letter per dock, not focus moving between docks, not \"the focused one\nanswers and every other declines\", not two cursors, not two scroll positions.\n\n# What to seat\n\n`WorkspacesContainerProvider::placed(\"workspaces.right\", RegionId::RightSidebar)` in\n`heca/src/app/startup.rs` — one line, the API that already exists (F003/P011/T021). The **content** is\nthe same (it comes from the shared store); what differs is per placement: mount id, scroll offset,\ncursor, and whether it holds focus.\n\n**It also exercises the kind/mount split for real**: `kind() == \"workspaces\"` for both, so `[keys.workspaces]`\nbinds once and applies to both, while cursor/scroll/focus stay separate. That is the property no unit\ntest makes visible.\n\n# What the user verifies in the app (tests are not verification here)\n\n1. `prefix+Shift+e` shows a letter over **each** dock; picking one focuses it and only it shows the ring.\n2. `j`/`k` move the cursor in the focused dock and **do nothing** in the other.\n3. `Enter` activates the focused dock's cursor row.\n4. `PageDown`/`Home`/`End` scroll the focused dock only; the other keeps its position.\n5. Right-click a row in either dock → that component's entries, acting on the row clicked.\n6. `Esc` returns the keyboard to the pane; typing then reaches the terminal again.\n7. Two cursors and two scroll positions survive a chrome rebuild (change a pane's git status).\n\n# Then\n\nAsk the user whether the second placement stays. It is one line either way; unlike last time it is not\nscaffolding — it is the only way anything above is observable, so removing it should be a deliberate\nchoice, not a default.\n\n# Acceptance\n\n- Two containers, independent focus / cursor / scroll, one shared binding table.\n- Whole workspace green, clippy 0 warnings.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
      "subtasks": [],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "startedAt": "",
      "completedAt": "",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-28T12:25:55.774Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T12:25:55.774Z"
