  "createdAt": "2026-07-28T12:21:31.986Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-07-29T13:38:21.562Z",
  "handoff": "# Session handoff — 2026-07-29\n\n## ⛔ READ FIRST — this phase is partly superseded\n\n**F003/P086 (`5SZ4E`) was created at the end of this session and changes decisions P085 was built\non.** Do not continue F003/P085/T356 without reading P086's description first. What changes:\n\n- `[keys.<kind>]` (shipped in P085/T355) becomes `[[keys.component]]` with `name` + optional\n  placement `id` — P086/T362.\n- The \"focusing a pane releases container focus\" rule added in P085/T352 **is a bug** and must come\n  out — it breaks `Space`. P086/T364.\n- `activate` / `peek`, declared as container actions in P085/T356 step 2, likely belong to the row\n  kinds instead. P086/T365.\n- `ActionMeta.default_binding`, made live in P085/T355, is deleted. P086/T366.\n- `sidebar_focus` retirement moves from P085/T356 step 5 to P086/T363; the context-menu move\n  (P085/T354 steps 5–7, parked in T356 step 4) moves to P086/T365.\n\n**Decide before resuming:** does T356 finish steps 3–5 as written, or hand the rest to P086?\n\n## Reason for stopping\n\nContext spent (~85%). Everything is committed on `feat/action-arg-declaration`, tree clean,\n**1046 tests, clippy 0 warnings**. Nothing half-built.\n\n## What the user HAS verified in the app (2026-07-29)\n\n**T352 — focus and cursor movement work.** `prefix+Shift+e` picks a dock, chrome focus routes the\nkeyboard, the focus layer resolves, `j`/`k` move the cursor. T352 is closed on that basis.\n\n**Not yet confirmed on that same path:** `Space`. It is **expected to be broken** — it hands the\nkeyboard to the pane instead of keeping it on the dock. Cause is understood and written up as\nP086/T364; do not re-diagnose it. Also unverified: the horizontal scroll keys (`Alt+PageUp` etc.,\nwhich need a row wider than the dock), the `.both()` scroll axes on the workspaces container (a\nhorizontal scrollbar may now appear), and the interactive-move drop change noted at the bottom.\n\n## Commits (9, oldest first)\n\n`3bfe4f6` grid-ui `nav_key` · `69b4158` focus is the mode + component contract + `[keys.<kind>]` +\nthe workspaces module move · `bfa8296` rows resolve through the retained tree · `51d7874` the model\nmoves off `AppState` · `898ca40` the component declares and performs its navigation · `a71d737`\n`CaretLeft` + its `ViewGlyph` mirror · `aa73bbe` one startup conflict report · `050f1f9` reload keeps\naction conflicts.\n\n## Task status\n\n- **T352 `VKF85`** — ✅ done, verified in the app.\n- **T359 `J88GP`** — ✅ done. `workspaces.right` seated in the right sidebar (`app/startup.rs`); the\n  workspaces `ScrollRegion` is `.both()`.\n- **T353 `R6E5J`** — ✅ done (`kind()`, `actions()`, `perform()`, `ProviderCx`).\n- **T354 `76N2N`** — ✅ done. Steps 5–7 were moved out; they are now P086/T365.\n- **T355 `NH962`** — ✅ done. Its config shape is replaced by P086/T362; the merge rules carry over.\n- **T356 `F3J4W`** — in progress. Steps 0, 1, 2 done. Steps 3–5 outstanding and partly superseded.\n- **T360 `58SE7`** — a plugin's own signals. Written up, not started.\n- **T361 `3PN6N`** (in P084) — tooltip appears after the pointer left, because a modal stops pointer\n  delivery and hover is edge-triggered. Written up, not started.\n\n## T356 — where it stands\n\n| step | state |\n|---|---|\n| 0 — delete fixed-row geometry | ✅ `bfa8296` |\n| 1 — model onto `WorkspacesContainerState` | ✅ `51d7874` |\n| 2 — declare + `perform` the navigation | ✅ `898ca40` (verified by the user) |\n| 3 — `w`/`p`/`c`/`x` onto the contract | outstanding; the user changed the letters (was `v`/`d`) |\n| 4 — context menu → `ContextTarget::Row` | moved to P086/T365 |\n| 5 — delete `SidebarNav` + the `sidebar_*` built-ins | outstanding; `sidebar_focus` moved to P086/T363 |\n\nStep 3's five verbs are still built-ins in `handlers.rs`, gated on `InputMode::SidebarNav`:\n`handle_sidebar_create_workspace` (`:1870`), `handle_sidebar_create_column` (`:1884`),\n`handle_sidebar_split_in_column` (`:1904`), `handle_sidebar_zoom_selected_column` (`:1914`),\n`handle_sidebar_delete_selected` (`:2145`). Their two helpers —\n`sidebar_selected_workspace_idx` / `sidebar_selected_column_target` — are pure reads of the\ncomponent's own model and move with them.\n\n**Open, and P086 lists it too:** which level owns `w` / `p` / `c` / `x`. `x` is clearly the row's;\n`w` (new workspace) is about no row; `p` and `c` are in between.\n\n## What is now true in the code\n\n- `heca/src/providers/workspaces/` is the component: `mod.rs`, `model.rs`, `model_tests.rs`.\n  `heca/src/sidebar/` is gone. No type in it names a side (`WorkspaceTree`, `WorkspaceRow`,\n  `PaneEntry`, `ColumnEntry`, `WorkspaceEntry`).\n- `AppState.sidebar_tree` no longer exists (77 fields → 76). Reads go through\n  `state.chrome_state.workspaces.tree()` / `.tree_mut()`.\n- The four keymap layers are one `keymap::Keymaps { flat, modes, components, triggers }`.\n- Conflicts are collected and reported once, at startup and after a reload\n  (`heca/src/app/conflicts.rs`). A built-in's id is refused outright and the rejected action gets no\n  key either.\n- The fixed-row sidebar hit-testing is gone; rows resolve through the retained tree.\n\n## Gotchas that cost time this session\n\n- **`WorkspacesContainerState::tree()` is a `RefCell`.** End the borrow before any call that reaches\n  back into the store, or it panics at runtime rather than failing to compile. Four borrows had to be\n  shortened; expect more when step 3 moves handlers in.\n- **`publish_sidebar_selection` → `selection_nav_key` is a deliberate single bridge** between the old\n  domain-typed selection and the generic cursor. It exists so there is exactly one place to delete in\n  step 5. Do not add a second.\n- **BSD `sed` has no `\\b`** — use Python for word-boundary renames.\n- **`every_glyph_name_has_a_mirror`** (in `heca-view-realize`) fails if a `Glyph` is added without\n  mirroring it into `heca-view`'s `ViewGlyph`. It caught exactly that this session.\n- `CaretLeft`'s codepoint `0xe138` is **inferred** from Phosphor's alphabetical layout — confirm in\n  the showcase glyph grid, as `CaretUp` already asks.\n- Do not run `cargo fmt` (repo rule). Rust skill review → clippy → commit, and wait for the user's\n  approval to commit.\n\n## One unverified judgement call\n\n`bfa8296` collapsed the interactive-move drop's four-arm match to three: a floating pane resolves as\n`ChromeDragItem::Pane`, `find_pane_location` does not find it in the tiled layout, and the fallback\nis what the floating-only arm already did (`Session::add_pane` uses the same default width on the\nsame workspace). Identical by inspection, but it is drag-and-drop — worth trying in the app.\n",
